  ["Who signs a structural calculation note?", "A structural engineer. At ESE, calculation notes are checked and signed by a partner structural engineer; ESE prepares the modelling, the drawings and the assumptions."],
  ["Does the calculation note replace the inspection?", "No. It justifies the set-up. Inspection and regulatory checks are carried out by an inspection body or an approved organisation, depending on the case."],
  ["How long does it take to get one?", "It depends on the complexity and on the information available (venue drawings, rigging point capacities, chosen equipment). The safest approach is to start it as soon as the layout and equipment are settled, before the final order."],
];
